RK809-5 PMIC — A1 REV1 ELECTRICAL PAGE,55,35,1.8
5V_SYS feeds VCC1..VCC9 and VCC_RTC. VCC_RTC must be highest or within 0.3V of highest PMIC supply.,55,48,1
BUCK1/2/3/4/5 use 0.47uH TDK SPM5030T-R47M-HZ; BUCK4 is populated but OTP-default OFF. Output capacitors follow RK809 application manual minimums; 2x47uF nominal shown, verify DC-bias effective capacitance.,55,62,1
BUCK3 feedback divider RH/RL remains DNP/TBD until LPDDR4X rail voltage and exact DRAM are frozen.,55,76,1
I2S/audio data and output pins are NC; CPP/CPN and VCC_CPVSS/CPVDD retain recommended charge-pump bypass capacitors. BATDIV, SNSP and SNSN are grounded because fuel gauge is not used.,55,92,1
VDC divider 100k/33k gives about 1.24V from 5V_SYS. EXT_EN drives external VDD_CPU regulator enable.,55,108,1
RESETB has required 100nF. SDA/SCL/INT/RESETB/CLK32K open-drain nets pull up to 1.8V domain.,55,124,1
PMIC output-to-SoC rail mapping is deliberately not frozen here; verify Rockchip EVB rail map and DDR choice before tying BUCK/LDO outputs to SoC.,55,140,1
